<!--
  Reloop Mixon 4: a Cadence profile from the online library (A208).

  SOURCE, and only this: the manufacturer's own MIDI documentation.
    MIXON 4 MIDI MAP (Reloop (reloop.com, Mixon 4 product page, Downloads tab), PDF created 2017-02-01; server Last-Modified 2017-02-02), pages 1-5 (binds from p1 and p2)
    https://www.reloop.com/media/custom/upload/Reloop-Mixon4_MIDI-Map.pdf
    Reloop Mixon 4 Instruction Manual (236534_Reloop_IM.pdf) (Reloop, undated), pages English control table, items 1-40 (used only to confirm what PARAMETER 1-/+, AUTO LOOP and LOOP ROLL do)
    https://www.reloop.com/media/catalog/product/pdf/2/3/6/236534_Reloop_IM.pdf
  No mapping file from any other application was read or used.

  status="manual": the message is the manufacturer's. Nobody has tried this map on the hardware
  yet. If a control does nothing, use Learn on that row and tell us at shlabs.contact@gmail.com.

  BEFORE YOU START: Connect by USB-B to the computer (the manual says USB and the iOS connector cannot be used at the same time). Put each deck's pads in HOT CUE mode (press the HOT CUE pad-mode button) so the pads send the hot-cue notes; other pad modes send other note numbers. Use the DECK button to switch a deck section between decks 1/3 (left) and 2/4 (right); deck 3/4 controls then send on MIDI channels 7/8. The MIDI map lists a SysEx 'Deck Restriction F0 0A 01 F7 Enable Deck 3&4' (and F0 0A 00 F7 to disable); it does not say which state is the default. Master and booth volume are hardware-only and send no MIDI.

  CADENCE'S CHOICES:
    PARAM - and PARAM + are bound to beat jump back and forward: the unit has no beat-jump buttons, and Reloop's manual gives PARAM that function in djay Pro.
    Not bound, because one target holds one control: CUE (deck transport) (Deck 1 column, n=4) (ch1.cuepad1), since HOT CUE mode PAD 1 (Deck 1 column, n=0) takes ch1.cuepad1; CUE (deck transport) (Deck 2 column, n=5) (ch2.cuepad1), since HOT CUE mode PAD 1 (Deck 2 column, n=1) takes ch2.cuepad1; CUE (deck transport) (Deck 3 column, n=6) (ch3.cuepad1), since HOT CUE mode PAD 1 (Deck 3 column, n=2) takes ch3.cuepad1; CUE (deck transport) (Deck 4 column, n=7) (ch4.cuepad1), since HOT CUE mode PAD 1 (Deck 4 column, n=3) takes ch4.cuepad1.

  LEFT OUT (no Cadence target): GAIN (trim) knob CC 00 (status column is blank in the doc; Cadence chN.gain is the volume fader, so not needed); FILTER FX button (note 01), FILTER Center / MAKRO FX centre notes (22/23); Crossfader CC 00 and CF CURVE CC 01 on n=0A (no Cadence target); CF ASSIGNMENT A/T/B switches (notes 04/05/06), FADER START up/down (shift notes 5D/5E); MASTER VOL and BOOTH VOL: marked HARDWARE, no MIDI (so no master.gain bind); SAMPLER volume CC 02 on n=0A; BACK button (note 01 on n=0A), SHIFT (note 03 on n=0A), QUANTIZE (note 02 on n=0A, hold 2 s); JOG TOUCH (note 07); EFFECT unit section on n=8/9: EFFECT 1-3 knobs CC 00-02, PARAMETER encoder CC 03 + push, ON 1-3 notes 00-02, TAP note 04; LOOP encoder CC 08 (relative; halves/doubles loop length) - Cadence loophalf/loopdbl are separate targets, so not bound; PITCH fader (pitch bend En) - cannot be bound; KEY LOCK (hold) 25, KEY SYNC 11, KEY SYNC double press 24, DECK 12, PHONO 13, LINE 14, VELOCITY 00, pad-mode buttons 16-1D; Pads in LOOP ROLL (08-0F), SAMPLER (10-17), SLICER (18-1F), CUE LOOP (20-27), SAVED LOOPS (28-2F), PITCH PLAY (30-37), SLICER LOOP (38-3F) modes; shifted pads (40-7F); All shifted messages; LED/VU/jog-LED outputs; RGB LED table; SysEx identify request

  A jog wheel that moves too fast or too slow: set its row to Fine, or invert it, in the dialog.
-->
